implementationPlan.description:
ADVERSARIAL SELF-REVIEW (load adversarial-self-review). Read the diff as an attacker who controls every guest byte. Try:
- a 0xFFFFFFFF length header;
- a frame delivered one byte at a time, and a valid frame after a poisoned one;
- output data that encodes a perfect observation frame;
- tool names that are Object.prototype members;
- args carrying identity keys equal to the binding;
- a worker binding asking for QA tools, and a binding with the wrong shape.
Confirm that:
- every refusal is a code with fixed text and never echoes guest content;
- the TOOLS table and every returned object are frozen;
- the diff contains nothing listed in the project's globalRails.forbiddenPatterns;
- ci.yml changed by exactly one command line, and no other existing file changed.
Fix anything you find. If any byte changed, re-run step 5's command and submit that fresh output as the evidence.

planningNotes.codebaseInsights:
scripts/local-runner modules are dependency-free ESM. They share these conventions:
- a MESSAGES map with an xxxError(code) helper (lifecycleError, bootstrapError, provisionError);
- isRecord and CONTROL helpers;
- Object.freeze on exported constants and results;
- fixed argv constants (GUEST_PROBES in guest-readiness.mjs);
- header comments citing the external facts they rely on.
Tests use node:test with assert/strict and are table-driven. Both IDE bundlers (moe-jetbrains/build.gradle.kts include("local-runner/**") and moe-vscode/scripts/bundle-assets.mjs) copy the whole directory minus test patterns, so the new module ships automatically. Owned instance names match /^moe-vm-[0-9a-f]{20}$/ (isOwnedInstanceName). The supervisor path is GUEST_LAYOUT.supervisor = /opt/moe/bin/moe-supervisor. The daemon tool schemas, all additionalProperties:false, are the source of the TOOLS table. get_handoff_history has no workerId and heartbeat has no taskId, so stamping must follow the table.
